<title>FINLAND: METRA'S WARTSILA WINS POWER PLANT ORDERS.</title>
<headline>METRA'S WARTSILA WINS POWER PLANT ORDERS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish diversified engineering group Metra Oy said in a statement on Thursday its Wartsila Diesel unit had won power plant orders from customers in Finland.</p>
<p>&quot;The power plants are sold to Ikaalinen and Sakyla,&quot; it said, adding the buyers of the Ikaalinen plant were a local electricity utility, Leppakosken Sahko Oy, and Neste Lampo Oy, part of state-controlled oil and energy group Neste Oy .</p>
<p>The buyers of the Sakyla plant were local utility Koylion-Sakylan sahko O and Neste Lampo, Metra said.</p>
<p>The value of the deals was not given. --Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
